<title>TAIWAN: TAIWAN BSPA BUYS 54,000 TONNES SOYBEANS AT TENDER.</title>
<headline>TAIWAN BSPA BUYS 54,000 TONNES SOYBEANS AT TENDER.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1997-08-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Taichung division of Taiwan's Breakfast Soybean Procurement Association bought a 54,000-tonne shipment of U.S. soybeans from Cargill at a tender on Friday, traders said.  </p>
<p>The association's Taichung division comprises Chia Hsin, Formosa Oilseed, Fwu Sow Grain, and Tay Shan.</p>
<p>The shipment was bought on a cost-and-freight basis.</p>
<p>Details for the tender are as follows:   Tonnes   Date/Location   Prices/Futures</p>
<p>	     Pacific N.W.</p>
<p>  54,000   Oct 1-15	  120.36 US cents/November</p>
